Encoded?:

I downloaded the enc and opened the file on VScode. They looked like Chinese/East Asian alphabets, but still seemed a bit fishy to me.

Hence, I opened dCode.fr, and ran it through the Cipher Identifier. It showed me that there was an approximately 20% chance that it could be a ROT8000 cipher, so I tried to decode it. However, the output the website gave me turned out to be random symbols.

Python Code?:

The line of text given plainly (not the enc file) was run by me on a python interpreter. I thought it would be in python since it was not defining any class or function, like they do in Java and C. (they might have it in python, but I don't have much experience with that language).

However, the code didn't run, and gave an error:

NameError: name ‘flag’ is not defined. Did you mean ‘float’?

Hence, it suggested that ‘flag’ did not exist in the code. Hence, I thought this would be a clue that we had to find the flag.

To decode it:

enc = "慣慤敭祻ㄶ形楴獟楮獴㌴摟潦弸強㤰扡㌷敽"

flag = ""
for c in enc:
    n = ord(c)
    flag += chr(n >> 8)
    flag += chr(n & 0xFF)

print(flag)

//In the output of this code, the flag was printed.


